.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH iron-vault-completions 1  "Iron Vault" "Iron Vault Manual"
.SH NAME
iron\-vault\-completions \- Print a shell completion script to stdout. It never contacts the service, so it also runs at build time
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBiron\-vault completions\fR [\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISHELL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a shell completion script to stdout. It never contacts the service, so it also runs at build time
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Use the admin socket at PATH instead of this installation\*(Aqs, for example one forwarded over SSH. Every client command takes it; `serve` refuses it, because the service always binds its own installation\*(Aqs socket
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISHELL\fR>
The shell to generate the script for
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bash: Bash, through the bash\-completion framework
.RE
